meta {
  name: Log in
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
    "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  // Protected requests send Authorization: Bearer {{token}}.
  if (res.status === 200) {
    bru.setVar("token", res.body.data.token);
  }
}

docs {
  # Log in

  Exchanges an email and password for an access token (JWT, HS256). Send this
  first: its post-response script stores the token as the runtime variable
  `token`, which every protected request sends as `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`.

  The token carries the user id (`sub`) and role code (`role`) only, and
  expires after `JWT_EXPIRES_IN` (default 1 hour). Write endpoints, and reads
  of everything except categories and products, require the `ADMIN` role.

  Set `adminEmail` in the environment and `adminPassword` as a secret
  environment variable (never committed); for development they are the
  `SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL` / `SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD` values from the web `.env`.

  ## Auth

  None.

  ## Body (JSON)

  | Field | Type | Required | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `email` | string | yes | Valid email; matched case-insensitively. |
  | `password` | string | yes | 1–72 characters. |

  ## Responses

  Every response uses the shared envelope `{ message, data, pagination }`;
  errors add `errors` (and `stack` outside production).

  ### 200 OK — signed in

  {
    "message": "Signed in",
    "data": {
      "token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...",
      "user": {
        "id": 1,
        "name": "Store",
        "lastName": "Administrator",
        "email": "admin@lpaecomms.test",
        "role": "ADMIN"
      }
    },
    "pagination": null
  }

  ### 400 Bad Request — malformed body

  {
    "message": "Some fields need attention.",
    "data": null,
    "pagination": null,
    "errors": [
      { "field": "email", "message": "Invalid email address" }
    ]
  }

  ### 401 Unauthorized — wrong credentials

  Returned alike for an unknown email, a wrong password, and an inactive or
  deleted account, so the response never reveals which emails exist.

  {
    "message": "Email or password is incorrect.",
    "data": null,
    "pagination": null,
    "errors": []
  }
}
